{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-3594" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{-{x}^{2}-8x-15}}\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064342/state.json" "file_sha256" "2a5012fe6b4135c3ae0e99aa9d38f15663383d26c93b194ca0697a1c82a54b39"} {"question" "q-3594" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we complete the square for the argument of the square root in the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-{x}^{2}-8x-15 & =-({x}^{2}+8x+15) \\\\  & =-({x}^{2}+2\\cdot 4x+[{4}^{2}-{4}^{2}]+15) \\\\  & =-((x+4)^{2}-1) \\\\  & =1-(x+4)^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above in the given integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{-{x}^{2}-8x-15}}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(x+4)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nThis resembles the basic integral for inverse sine:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡u+C\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of $u$ as the variable, we have $(x+4).$\n\nSo, let's perform the substitution\n\n$$\nu=x+4.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we get \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nFinally, we write the integral in terms of $u,$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{-{x}^{2}-8x-15}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(x+4)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡u+C \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(x+4)+C.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064342/state.json" "file_sha256" "2a5012fe6b4135c3ae0e99aa9d38f15663383d26c93b194ca0697a1c82a54b39"} {"question" "q-3594" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064342/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4aaaee319d0a15eeb2643506c2c9363972155fb90cfecd536c077b8d91423680"} {"question" "q-3594" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064342/state.json" "file_sha256" "2a5012fe6b4135c3ae0e99aa9d38f15663383d26c93b194ca0697a1c82a54b39"} {"question" "q-3594" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{x-4}{4})+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\frac{x-4}{4})+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(x+4)+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(x-4)+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(x+4)+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064342/state.json" "file_sha256" "2a5012fe6b4135c3ae0e99aa9d38f15663383d26c93b194ca0697a1c82a54b39"} {"question" "q-3594" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(x+4)+C"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064342/state.json" "file_sha256" "2a5012fe6b4135c3ae0e99aa9d38f15663383d26c93b194ca0697a1c82a54b39"} {"question" "q-114929" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int \\frac{1}{|x+2|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+4x+3}}\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064342/state.json" "file_sha256" "2a5012fe6b4135c3ae0e99aa9d38f15663383d26c93b194ca0697a1c82a54b39"} {"question" "q-114929" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we complete the square for the expression inside the square root:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+4x+3 & ={x}^{2}+2\\cdot 2x+({2}^{2}-{2}^{2})+3 \\\\  & =({x}^{2}+4x+4)-4+3 \\\\  & =(x+2)^{2}-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above in the given integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{|x+2|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+4x+3}}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\frac{1}{|x+2|\\sqrt{(x+2)^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nThis resembles the basic integral for inverse secant:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}u=\\text{arcsec}\\,u+C\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of $u$ as the variable, we have $x+2.$\n\nSo, let's perform the substitution \n\n$$\nu=x+2.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nFinally, we write the integral in terms of $u,$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{|x+2|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+4x+3}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{|x+2|\\sqrt{(x+2)^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\text{arcsec}\\,u+C \\\\  & =\\text{arcsec}(x+2)+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064342/state.json" "file_sha256" "2a5012fe6b4135c3ae0e99aa9d38f15663383d26c93b194ca0697a1c82a54b39"} {"question" "q-114929" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064342/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4aaaee319d0a15eeb2643506c2c9363972155fb90cfecd536c077b8d91423680"} {"question" "q-114929" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064342/state.json" "file_sha256" "2a5012fe6b4135c3ae0e99aa9d38f15663383d26c93b194ca0697a1c82a54b39"} {"question" "q-114929" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2\\,\\text{arcsec}(\\frac{x+2}{2})+C"] ["math" "2\\,\\text{arcsec}(\\frac{x-2}{2})+C"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{arcsec}(2(x+2))+C"] ["math" "\\text{arcsec}(x+2)+C"] ["math" "\\text{arcsec}(x-2)+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064342/state.json" "file_sha256" "2a5012fe6b4135c3ae0e99aa9d38f15663383d26c93b194ca0697a1c82a54b39"} {"question" "q-114929" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\text{arcsec}(x+2)+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064342/state.json" "file_sha256" "2a5012fe6b4135c3ae0e99aa9d38f15663383d26c93b194ca0697a1c82a54b39"} {"question" "q-348528" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{\\sqrt{2}-3}^{-1}\\frac{6}{|x+3|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+6x+8}}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064342/state.json" "file_sha256" "2a5012fe6b4135c3ae0e99aa9d38f15663383d26c93b194ca0697a1c82a54b39"} {"question" "q-348528" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we complete the square for the expression inside the square root:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+6x+8 & ={x}^{2}+2\\cdot 3x+({3}^{2}-{3}^{2})+8 \\\\  & =({x}^{2}+2\\cdot 3x+{3}^{2})-9+8 \\\\  & =(x+3)^{2}-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the given integral, we get\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{\\sqrt{2}-3}^{-1}\\frac{6}{|x+3|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+6x+8}}\\,\\text{d}x=6{\\int }_{\\sqrt{2}-3}^{-1}\\frac{1}{|x+3|\\sqrt{(x+3)^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nThis resembles the basic integral for inverse secant:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}u=\\text{arcsec}\\,u+C\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of $u$ as the variable, we have $(x+3).$\n\nSo, let's perform the substitution\n\n$$\nu=x+3.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nLet's use the table below to change the limits from $x$ to $u.$\n\n| $x$ | $\\sqrt{2}-3$ | $-1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $\\sqrt{2}$ | $2$ |\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\sqrt{2}-3}^{-1}\\frac{6}{|x+3|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+6x+8}}\\,\\text{d}x & =6{\\int }_{\\sqrt{2}}^{2}\\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =6\\,\\text{arcsec}\\,u\\,{|}_{\\sqrt{2}}^{2} \\\\  & =6(\\text{arcsec}(2)-\\text{arcsec}(\\sqrt{2})) \\\\  & =6(\\frac{\\pi }{3}-\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064342/state.json" "file_sha256" "2a5012fe6b4135c3ae0e99aa9d38f15663383d26c93b194ca0697a1c82a54b39"} {"question" "q-348528" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064342/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4aaaee319d0a15eeb2643506c2c9363972155fb90cfecd536c077b8d91423680"} {"question" "q-348528" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064342/state.json" "file_sha256" "2a5012fe6b4135c3ae0e99aa9d38f15663383d26c93b194ca0697a1c82a54b39"} {"question" "q-348528" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\pi}{2}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064342/state.json" "file_sha256" "2a5012fe6b4135c3ae0e99aa9d38f15663383d26c93b194ca0697a1c82a54b39"} {"question" "q-348555" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{-4}^{-3}\\frac{6}{{x}^{2}+8x+17}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064342/state.json" "file_sha256" "2a5012fe6b4135c3ae0e99aa9d38f15663383d26c93b194ca0697a1c82a54b39"} {"question" "q-348555" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we complete the square in the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+8x+17 & ={x}^{2}+2\\cdot 4x+({4}^{2}-{4}^{2})+17 \\\\  & =({x}^{2}+2\\cdot 4x+{4}^{2})-16+17 \\\\  & =(x+4)^{2}+1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the denominator, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{6}{{x}^{2}+8x+17}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{6}{(x+4)^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =6\\int \\frac{1}{1+(x+4)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis resembles the basic integral for inverse tangent:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u+C\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of $u$ as the variable, we have $(x+4).$\n\nSo, let's perform the substitution\n\n$$\nu=x+4.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nLet's use the table below to change the limits from $x$ to $u.$\n\n| $x$ | $-4$ | $-3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $1$ |\n\nFinally, we write the integral in terms of $u,$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-4}^{-3}\\frac{6}{{x}^{2}+8x+17}\\,\\text{d}x & =6{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =6\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u\\,{|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =6(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(1)-\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =6(\\frac{\\pi }{4}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\pi }{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064342/state.json" "file_sha256" "2a5012fe6b4135c3ae0e99aa9d38f15663383d26c93b194ca0697a1c82a54b39"} {"question" "q-348555" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064342/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4aaaee319d0a15eeb2643506c2c9363972155fb90cfecd536c077b8d91423680"} {"question" "q-348555" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064342/state.json" "file_sha256" "2a5012fe6b4135c3ae0e99aa9d38f15663383d26c93b194ca0697a1c82a54b39"} {"question" "q-348555" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{3\\pi}{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064342/state.json" "file_sha256" "2a5012fe6b4135c3ae0e99aa9d38f15663383d26c93b194ca0697a1c82a54b39"} {"question" "q-348571" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{5}^{5+\\sqrt{3}}\\frac{7}{{x}^{2}-10x+26}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064342/state.json" "file_sha256" "2a5012fe6b4135c3ae0e99aa9d38f15663383d26c93b194ca0697a1c82a54b39"} {"question" "q-348571" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we complete the square in the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-10x+26 & ={x}^{2}-2\\cdot 5x+({5}^{2}-{5}^{2})+26 \\\\  & =({x}^{2}-2\\cdot 5x+{5}^{2})-25+26 \\\\  & =(x-5)^{2}+1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the denominator, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{7}{{x}^{2}-10x+26}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{7}{(x-5)^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =7\\int \\frac{1}{1+(x-5)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis resembles the basic integral for inverse tangent:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u+C\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of $u$ as the variable, we have $(x-5).$\n\nSo, let's perform the substitution\n\n$$\nu=x-5.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nLet's use the table below to change the limits from $x$ to $u.$\n\n| $x$ | $5$ | $5+\\sqrt{3}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $\\sqrt{3}$ |\n\nFinally, we write the integral in terms of $u,$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{5}^{5+\\sqrt{3}}\\frac{7}{{x}^{2}-10x+26}\\,\\text{d}x & =7{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}}\\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =7\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u\\,{|}_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}} \\\\  & =7(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡\\sqrt{3}-\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =7(\\frac{\\pi }{3}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{7\\pi }{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064342/state.json" "file_sha256" "2a5012fe6b4135c3ae0e99aa9d38f15663383d26c93b194ca0697a1c82a54b39"} {"question" "q-348571" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064342/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4aaaee319d0a15eeb2643506c2c9363972155fb90cfecd536c077b8d91423680"} {"question" "q-348571" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064342/state.json" "file_sha256" "2a5012fe6b4135c3ae0e99aa9d38f15663383d26c93b194ca0697a1c82a54b39"} {"question" "q-348571" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{7\\pi}{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064342/state.json" "file_sha256" "2a5012fe6b4135c3ae0e99aa9d38f15663383d26c93b194ca0697a1c82a54b39"}] "usage" {} "basis" 2106 "retractions" [] "immutable_answers" [] "immutable_fields" [] "no_history" []}
